    {
      "page": 2,
      "title": "TabPFN · Pretrained prediction rules for tabular data (v3: arXiv, 2026)",
      "notes": "Source: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.13986 §2.5, PDF page 10: more than 8 trillion tokens, not datasets. Official TabPFN 8.2.0: https://github.com/PriorLabs/TabPFN/blob/main/src/tabpfn/finetuning/finetuned_base.py. The archived initial-FT ablation in EXP77 uses AdamW, learning rate 1e-5, 10 fixed epochs, context/query cross-entropy; current displayed PFN results use no IDS FT. The v3 decoder weights context one-hot labels, so old-class examples remain necessary in the inference context. Validation is inside the 1000 revealed-label budget; no test tuning."
    },
    {
      "page": 3,
      "title": "v3 architecture",
      "notes": "Original Figure 5, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.13986#page=6. Native PPTX crop excludes the original caption. Labels and source remain in speaker notes. First three stages: feature grouping/cell embedding; target-aware column distribution embedding; row-level feature aggregation. Plain language deliberately omits implementation dimensions."
    },
    {
      "page": 4,
      "title": "v3 architecture",
      "notes": "Same Figure 5, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.13986#page=6; no visible caption by user request. ICL attends to training/context keys; many-class decoder uses attention-weighted one-hot context labels. This is learned contextual relevance, not merely raw-feature nearest-neighbour distance. Context determines available class labels."
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "title": "Evaluation scenario",
      "notes": "Displayed XGB and no-FT PFN use the same released IDs as EXP76/77. XGB cumulatively retrains; PFN retains original pretrained weights and cumulative context. Initial and repeated IDS FT ablations remain in the experiment archive and are not shown. This small-label scenario supports slides6 and8; slide7 instead uses100000 training rows and separate proposed-model validation, detailed on pages9 and10. Stage order chronological, within-stage sample counts descending. Main score is the FINAL state on ALL held-out rows, not pooled stage predictions. Final evaluation convention: EXP81 seed43 permutation of test row indices independent of labels, query batch8192. PFN probabilities and DistPFN correction recomputed on all mixed batches. Row-wise XGB/proposed/Boost predictions retained only after exact mixed-query audit; any mismatching model is fully reevaluated. Budget10/20/50/200/400 PFN predictions checked with the same audit. Original-order results preserved in EXP77/78/79/80. No model tuning on test. Source: tabpfn/results/v7/exp81/20261016_025421_mixed_query_final_s43_b6ba1d34/results.json"
    },
    {
      "page": 6,
      "title": "Results",
      "notes": "EXP77 final-model full-test results: tabpfn/results/v7/exp77/20261015_230535_initialft10_finalfull_s43_2eb2237d/results.json. Two displayed methods: XGB cumulative retraining from scratch at every stage and original pretrained TabPFN with cumulative context, no IDS fine-tuning. Initial-FT results are retained in EXP77/EXP78, removed from slides 6 and 7 at user request. Slide 6 alone reports later-stage update cost: GPU-synchronized context selection + model construction + fit summed AFTER the initial stage; initial preparation and all inference excluded. Single seed 43. A separate EXP78 label-budget artifact covers 100/50/20/10 new examples per class, with initial 1000 fixed. Final evaluation convention: EXP81 seed43 permutation of test row indices independent of labels, query batch8192. PFN probabilities and DistPFN correction recomputed on all mixed batches. Row-wise XGB/proposed/Boost predictions retained only after exact mixed-query audit; any mismatching model is fully reevaluated. Budget10/20/50/200/400 PFN predictions checked with the same audit. Original-order results preserved in EXP77/78/79/80. No model tuning on test. Source: tabpfn/results/v7/exp81/20261016_025421_mixed_query_final_s43_b6ba1d34/results.json"
    },
    {
      "page": 7,
      "title": "100k training samples · Proposed model and SOTA",
      "notes": "User-requested replacement of the small-label SOTA comparison after EXP82 diagnosis. EXP79/81 final-stage models, same complete test as the small-data evaluation, mixed query convention, no retraining or threshold tuning for reevaluation. Every method uses a 100000-row training pool (75000 Benign +25000 attacks), with natural and availability-capped uniform attack allocations. Proposed Global context is approximately50000 rows; its separate validation is additional to the training pool. Exact stage and validation counts are on appendix pages9 and10. BoostPFN uses v1; other PFN methods use v3, no IDS weight FT. Results do not establish consistent superiority: proposed is highest at CIC2018 uniform79.00%, while XGB leads both ToN allocations. Improve expert construction and routing using held-out training/validation evidence. Small-label comparison was removed from presentation at user request, not invalidated: EXP82 reproduced52.89% and identical probabilities with the695-row Global-only control. tabpfn/results/v7/exp81/20261016_025421_mixed_query_final_s43_b6ba1d34/results.json Final evaluation convention: EXP81 seed43 permutation of test row indices independent of labels, query batch8192. PFN probabilities and DistPFN correction recomputed on all mixed batches. Row-wise XGB/proposed/Boost predictions retained only after exact mixed-query audit; any mismatching model is fully reevaluated. Budget10/20/50/200/400 PFN predictions checked with the same audit. Original-order results preserved in EXP77/78/79/80. No model tuning on test. Source: tabpfn/results/v7/exp81/20261016_025421_mixed_query_final_s43_b6ba1d34/results.json"
